# keyed_replace_vs_distinct -- leg B.
#
# An edge rule into a `key(1)` head. The question is what an IDENTICAL value
# re-arriving on the same key does: R7 boundary diffing says a keyed write of a
# row that is already there produces no delta, which is distinctUntilChanged's
# whole contract. `reading` is `log keep(all)`, so the duplicate arrivals
# themselves are all visible and only the keyed head is expected to swallow
# them.

rel reading(sensor: text, value: text) log keep(all).
rel current(sensor: text, value: text) key(1).

current(Sensor, Value) <+ reading(Sensor, Value).
